  "raw_text": "80\n\nIwanka tnatka sât sât\n \n–\n \nall sorts of ways of living, all sorts of customs, diverse customs\n \n/ todo tipo\n\nde formas de vi\nvir\n, todo tipo de costumbres, costumbres diversas\n\nIwi uplika nani\n \n–\n \npeople living\n \n/ gente\n \nque\n \nvive\n, habitante\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nJ\nirimaya\n \n18:11\n):\n \nJerusalem ra iwi uplika nani\n \n–\n \npeople living in Jerusalem, inhabitants of Jerusalem\n \n/ personas\n\nque viven en Jerusalén,\n \nhabitantes de Jerusalén\n)\n\nIws\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \nsit, sit down\n \n/ siéntate\n\nLilia iwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto live happily, to live joyfully\n \n/ vivir felizmente, vivir alegremente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfg5\n):\n \nJehova Adam bara ai luhpia nani ra sanska yaban lilia ban kaia ra naha tasba ra iwbia\n \n–\n \nJehovah gave the\nopportunity to Adam and his children to live happily on earth forever\n \n/ Jehová le dio la oportunidad a Adán y a sus hijos de\nvivir felices en la tierra para siempre)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfg9\n):\n \nWitin ba Gâd kum lilia sa bara want sa upla nani ba lilia iwbia\n \n–\n \nHe is a happy God and wants people to live\nhappily\n \n/ Es un Dios feliz y quiere que las personas vivan felices)\n\nMâyara iwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto decline, to lower, to decline to a lower position\n \n/ declinar, disminuir, bajar, descender a una\nposición más baja\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-08/19\n):\n \nwan wîna tara karnika ba mâyara iwan sa kaka\n \n–\n \nif our physical strength has declined\n \n/ si nuestra\nfuerza física ha disminuido)\n\nTâ iwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto astound, to marvel, to be amazed, to surprise\n \n/ asombrar, maravillar, sorprender\n\n(Construct:\n \nTâi iwaia\n \n–\n \nto astound/marvel/amaze or surprise me\n \n/ asombrar/maravillar o sorprenderme;\n \nTâm iwaia\n \n–\n \nto\nastound/marvel/amaze or surprise you\n \n/ sorprenderte/maravillarte o sorprenderte)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh-db-Mark 5:42\n):\n \nTuktika aisika nani ba tâ pali iwan\n \n–\n \nThe child’s parents were amazed (NWT\n-\n“in ecstasy”)\n \n/ Los\npadres del niño estaban asombrados (\nTNM\n-\"en éxtasis\"))\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-01/19\n):\n \nPal bîla nani aisan ba, king ba pain wali tâ iwan.\n \n–\n \nListening well, the king was amazed at the words\nPaul said.\n \n/ Escuchando bien, el rey se sorprendió de las palabras que dijo Pablo.)\n\nTasba ra iwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto live on earth\n \n/ vivir en la tierra\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \ntasba ra iwaia bîla kaiki nani ba\n \n–\n \nthose hoping to live on earth\n \n/ aquellos que esperan vivir en la tierra)\n\nUpla iwras\n \n–\n \nuninhabited, no person living,\n \nn\no person dwelling\n \n/ deshabitada,\n \nnadie\n \nviv\ni\ne\nndo\n,\n \nnadie\n \nhabita\nndo\n\nUpla iwras tasbaya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nuninhabited land, wilderness\n \n/ tierra deshabitada, desierto\n\nJan\n \n(\ndb,dba\n;\n \nJon\n-dbta,lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nJohn\n \n(Bible books) / Juan (libros bíblicos)\n\nJan Tatahbra\n \n–\n \nJohn the Baptist\n \n/ Juan el Bautista\n\nJasua\n \n(\ndb,dba,dbta\n;\n \nJosua\n-bw\n)\n \n–\n \nJoshua\n \n(Bible book) / Josué (libro bíblico)\n\nJehova\n \n(\nsln\n \nspelling;\n \nbw\n \nuses both\n \nJehova\n \n459 times and\n \nYehova\n \n1 time;\n \nsln\n \nuses\n \nJehova\n \n727 times;\n \ndictu\n \noffers\naltnerate spellings\n \nJehoba\n,\nYehova\n \n/ ortografía\n \nsln\n;\n \nbw\n \nusa tanto a\n \nJehová\n \n459 veces como a\n \nYehova\n \n1 vez;\n \nsln\n \nusa a\n\nJehová\n \n727 veces;\n \ndictu\n \nofrece deletreos alternativos\n \nJoba, Yehova\n)\n \n–\n \nJehovah\n \n/ Jehová\n\nJehova asla takanka\n \n–\n \nJehovah’s organization\n \n/\n \nO\nrganización de Jehová\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n10/20\n):\n \nSturi yamni smalkaia dukiara, Jehova asla takanka ba d\nî\na tnatka nani yus munan sa?\n \n–\n \nIn order to\n\npreach the good news, what methods has Jehovah’s\n \norganization used?\n \n/ Para predicar las buenas nuevas, ¿qué métodos\n\nha utilizado la organización de Jehová?\n)\n\nJehova asla takanka ra wark nani briaia\n \n–\n \nto have privileges in Jehovah’s organization\n \n/ tener privilegios\n\nen la organización de Jehová\n\nJehova\n \nw\nitniska nani\n \n–\n \nJehovah’s Witnesses\n \n/ Testigos de Jehová\n\nJehova\n \nw\nitnis kum\n \n–\n \none of Jehovah’s Witnesses\n \n/\n \nu\nno de los Testigos de Jehová\n\nJehova\n \nw\nitniska nani Tâ Bri Daknika ba\n \n–\n \nGoverning Body of Jehovah’s Witnesses\n \n/ Cuerpo Gobernante de los\n\nTestigos de Jehová\n\nJems\n \n(\ndb\n,\ndba,dbta,lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nJames\n \n(Bible book)\n \n/\n \nSantiago\n \n(libro bíblico)\n\nJinja\n \n(\nbc,dict,dictu\n;\n \nGinja\n-\ndictu\n-\nalt\n,\n \nSinsa\n-\ndictu\n-\nalt\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nginger\n \n/ jengibre\n\nJirimaya\n \n(\ndb\n;\n \nJirimaia\n-\ndba\n;\n \nJeremaia\n-\nbw\n;\n \nJere\nmí\nas\n-\ndbta\n)\n \n–\n \nJeremiah\n \n(Bible book)\n \n/\n \nJeremías\n \n(libro bíblico)\n\nJisas\n \n(\ndb,bm,km,lv\n,bh,fy,kt,jl,fg,my,ll,t,rsg14\n,dictu\n-\nalt\n;\n \nJisus\n-\nlrw,dictu\n,dict\n;\n \nJisus\n,\nJisas\n-\ndbta,dba\n;\n \nDisas\n-\ndict\n-\nalt\n;\n \nDisus\n-\ndict\n-\n\nalt\n)\n \n–\n \nJesu\ns\n \n/ Jesús\n\nJisas Pruan Kupia Kraukanka\n \n(\na/t:\n \nKraist Pruan Kupia Kraukanka\n)\n \n–\n \nMemorial of Jesus’\n \nDeath\n \n/\n \nConmemoración\n\nde la muerte de Jesús\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n):\n \nKakairikam kum Jisas Pruan Kupia Kraukanka ra waia paiwanka brin, bara kau nu takan daukan wal kli\n\naisas\n \n–\n \nFollow up with an acquaintance who accepted your invitation to attend the Memorial\n \n/\n \nVuelva a hablar con un\n\nconocido que aceptó la invitación a la Conmemoración y mostró interés)",
